			<personalityDescription>Asko sees morality as a luxury he can&apos;t afford. If there&apos;s a faster, more efficient way to get ahead - no matter how brutal - he&apos;ll take it without hesitation or regret. Asko knows war is ugly, merciless, brutal. But when he finds an enemy who fights with skill, honor, and intelligence, he acknowledges them. Because if there&apos;s nothing but slaughter and chaos, then what&apos;s the point of fighting at all? </personalityDescription>
