			<personalityDescription>Milada charges into danger without a second thought, unshaken by enemy fire or overwhelming odds. She believes fear is a distraction and meets every challenge with unwavering resolve. Milada doesn&apos;t recite poetry for theatrics. She does it because it&apos;s how she copes. The right words make chaos feel structured, give meaning to the things she&apos;d rather not think about. If she stops speaking, if she stops finding words for the war, then she&apos;ll have to admit that none of it ever had meaning to begin with. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 38%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Charges in without hesitation. Treats fear as noise, not warning.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
