			<personalityDescription>Stephanie has a habit of stretching the truth - sometimes a little, sometimes a lot. Whether it&apos;s exaggerating her accomplishments, fudging numbers, or making promises she can&apos;t keep, she always finds a way to make herself look better than she really is. Stephanie doesn&apos;t deal in half-truths or carefully worded pleasantries. She calls things exactly as she sees them, no matter how uncomfortable it makes people - because, to her, honesty is more valuable than diplomacy. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 38%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Shines up mediocrity like it&apos;s gold - good at making nothing sound impressive.&lt;br&gt;- Says the thing everyone else avoids - loud, clear, and on purpose.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
