			<personalityDescription>Loan never does anything halfway. Whether it&apos;s firepower, preparation, or just sheer intensity, he goes all-in, often pushing beyond what&apos;s necessary - or even reasonable. The object in Loan&apos;s possession isn&apos;t sentimental - it&apos;s survival. A reminder of who he used to be, of a promise he couldn&apos;t keep, of a person he once knew. He doesn&apos;t talk about it, doesn&apos;t let anyone touch it, doesn&apos;t explain why he refuses to part with it. Some wounds don&apos;t bleed, but they never heal either. </personalityDescription>
