			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Wars aren&apos;t just won with firepower - they&apos;re won with leverage, alliances, and well-placed words. Sylvestre understands that diplomacy is just another battlefield, and he wield it with the same precision as a well-aimed PPC shot. Sylvestre doesn&apos;t just like to lead - he needs to. Every decision, every plan, every battle has to go his way, and he expects absolute obedience. Anything less is just another problem to be dealt with. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 52%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Treats diplomacy as warfare. Targets alliances with tactical precision.&lt;br&gt;- Must be in charge. Demands obedience - anything else is interference.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
