			<personalityDescription>Manole doesn&apos;t see the point in fighting for a bigger slice of the pie when he&apos;s already got enough to get by. Others can stress over promotions and prestige - he&apos;ll take his time, do what&apos;s necessary, and enjoy life without all the extra pressure. Even in the heat of war, Manole never loses sight of the people fighting beside him. Whether it&apos;s sharing supplies, covering for a comrade&apos;s mistake, or simply checking in, he proves that true leadership starts with empathy. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 51%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Knows their lane. Won&apos;t leave it. Won&apos;t look up.&lt;br&gt;- Leads with empathy. The kind we need more of.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
