			<personalityDescription>To Kung, control isn&apos;t about leadership - it&apos;s about domination. He micromanages, manipulates, and enforces his will through intimidation or force. If someone steps out of line, they&apos;ll regret it. Trying to anticipate Kung&apos;s next move is a waste of time. He follows no pattern, sticks to no script, and seems to act purely on instinct - sometimes brilliant, sometimes reckless, but always unpredictable. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Leads through domination. Controls through fear, force, or pressure.&lt;br&gt;- Wild card. Dangerous. Might save the mission - or sink it.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
