			<personalityDescription>To Mary, hesitation is just another word for failure. She throws caution aside, charging headlong into danger with raw aggression and an utter disregard for self-preservation. If survival means second-guessing, then maybe survival isn&apos;t worth it. Mary sees every situation as a puzzle to be solved, every person as a piece to be placed. She never acts without purpose, ensuring that each decision moves her one step closer to her ultimate goal. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 51%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Ignores self-preservation. Sees hesitation as death. Risk of early burnout.&lt;br&gt;- Treats people like game pieces. Every action serves a greater plan.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
