			<personalityDescription>Hasbi rarely takes others seriously, rolling his eyes at concerns he doesn&apos;t find valid. Whether it&apos;s a risky plan, a personal grievance, or a suggestion he thinks is dumb, he shuts it down with a snide remark and moves on. Hasbi tells stories not because they&apos;re entertaining, but because he refuses to let people be forgotten. He speaks of old battles, fallen comrades, places that don&apos;t exist anymore. He remembers so that others won&apos;t have to. Or maybe, because he knows no one else will. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Eye-rolls and shutdowns. Doesn&apos;t bother pretending to care.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
