			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Beppe thrives on impulse, driven by an unshakable belief that momentum is more important than caution. Plans are for people who doubt themselves - Beppe simply does, and lets the universe catch up. Beppe doesn&apos;t chew gum for fun. They chew because if they stop, their jaw clenches, their stomach knots, and the ghosts get a little louder. They&apos;ve tasted blood, smoke, and the bitter air of burning cities. But as long as they&apos;re chewing, as long as they focus on that single, repetitive motion, they can pretend - just for a little while - that things are normal. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 55%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Momentum addict. Planning seen as weakness. Lets consequences catch up later.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
