			<personalityDescription>Antoniya never stops - because stopping means thinking, and thinking means facing the ghosts that haunt them. They fight, train, and push themself beyond exhaustion, running from a past that never quite lets them rest. Antoniya hums to fill the silence where voices used to be. The comrades who didn&apos;t make it back, the allies lost on distant battlefields, the old commanders who once barked orders over the radio. If they hum loud enough, maybe they won&apos;t have to hear their ghosts whispering back. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 50%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Pushing past exhaustion to outrun something deeper. Momentum masks pain.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
