			<personalityDescription>Ferah doesn&apos;t just look down on others - they barely acknowledge them. They see themself as superior in every way, treating allies as tools and enemies as annoyances. If someone disagrees with them, it&apos;s because they&apos;re too stupid to understand why they&apos;re right. Ferah doesn&apos;t believe in rushing headfirst into a situation - they dissect it first. They consider risks, weigh benefits, and ensure that every move they make is deliberate, calculated, and designed for maximum impact. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 48%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Barely acknowledges teammates. Sees people as tools or distractions.&lt;br&gt;- Dissects every situation before stepping in. No surprises.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
