			<personalityDescription>Lauryn doesn&apos;t waste time on fair deals when an unfair one gets her more. She plays on desperation, weaknesses, and ambition, twisting every situation to ensure that, in the end, Lauryn is the one who profits most. Lauryn&apos;s indifference isn&apos;t an act - it&apos;s survival. She&apos;s seen too much, lost too much, and learned that the only way to endure is to stop feeling altogether. The universe burns, but she stopped worrying about the flames a long time ago. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- If theres a win to be had, they&apos;ll take the lion&apos;s share and call it fair.&lt;br&gt;- Hollow eyes. Doesnt hate you - just can&apos;t be bothered to.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
