			<personalityDescription>Quigley doesn&apos;t just look down on others - he barely acknowledges them. He sees himself as superior in every way, treating allies as tools and enemies as annoyances. If someone disagrees with him, it&apos;s because they&apos;re too stupid to understand why he&apos;s right. Quigley feels everything - the pain, the fear, the suffering of those around him. It weighs on him, but he refuses to turn away, even when caring too much becomes a liability in a universe that rewards cruelty. </personalityDescription>
