			<personalityDescription>John doesn&apos;t just hold his ground - he digs in so deep that nothing short of  disaster can move him. Changing his mind is as likely as shifting a mountain by sheer force of will. John has taken so many lives. Bombed forests, scorched farmland, turned green fields into battlefields. So he grows plants - not to balance the scales (nothing could), but to remind himself that creation is still possible. That not everything has been reduced to ash. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 46%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Digs in deep. Unmoving, unchanging, unyielding.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
