			<personalityDescription>Adam knows exactly what to say to get people on his side, but his words rarely match his true intentions. He smiles, flatters, and makes promises, but beneath it all, he&apos;s only looking out for himself. Adam doesn&apos;t just talk tech - he hides in it. Talk about casualties? He pivots to weapon diagnostics. Discuss a lost battle? He starts breaking down armor slag statistics. The moment he stops analyzing specs and stats, the reality of war starts creeping in. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 48%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- All charm, no substance. Says the right things, means none of them.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
