			<personalityDescription>There&apos;s determination, and then there&apos;s Finlay. Once they make a decision, no amount of logic, pleading, or even superior orders will make them budge. Whether it&apos;s admirable or infuriating depends on who you ask. Finlay&apos;s indifference isn&apos;t an act - it&apos;s survival. They&apos;ve seen too much, lost too much, and learned that the only way to endure is to stop feeling altogether. The universe burns, but they stopped worrying about the flames a long time ago. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 39%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Logic bounces off. Orders ignored if they conflict with conviction.&lt;br&gt;- Hollow eyes. Doesnt hate you - just can&apos;t be bothered to.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
