			<personalityDescription>Gilbert doesn&apos;t just take charge - he owns every situation he steps into. His presence alone demands compliance, and he has little patience for those who hesitate to fall in line. Gilbert jokes because if he stops, he might have to actually think about what&apos;s happening. The losses, the suffering, the weight of everything - it&apos;s too much. So instead, he cracks another joke, forces another grin, and keeps moving like nothing&apos;s wrong. </personalityDescription>
