			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Distractions are for other people - Jack doesn&apos;t indulge them. He keeps his attention locked onto the task at hand, tuning out anything that doesn&apos;t push him closer to success. Jack used to follow orders, used to stick to the doctrine. But he&apos;s watched it fail, seen people die because they did what they were told instead of what actually needed to be done. Now? He adapts, or he dies. &quot;You want me to follow the plan exactly? Then tell me how that worked out for the last poor bastard who tried it.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Tunes out distractions completely. Sees only the path forward.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
