			<personalityDescription>Bob sees rules as obstacles, not boundaries. If there&apos;s a shortcut to be taken or a loophole to exploit, they&apos;ll find it - ethics and fairness be damned. Trusting Bob is a mistake most people only make once. They weave a careful web of half-truths and false assurances, making it nearly impossible to tell where their real motives lie - until they&apos;ve already gotten what they wanted. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Treats rules like suggestions. Never plays clean.&lt;br&gt;- Smiles like a friend, schemes like an enemy. Don&apos;t turn your back.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
