			<personalityDescription>Toshikazu doesn&apos;t just want to prove himself - he needs to. He throws himself into battles, pushes limits, and takes on risks that others would shy away from, desperate to show he&apos;s worthy of something bigger. Toshikazu has watched people fall to their deaths. He&apos;s seen what&apos;s left when they hit the ground. He remembers the silence right before impact. His fear isn&apos;t irrational - it&apos;s experience. &quot;You ever hear the sound someone makes when they realize there&apos;s no way back up? I have.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 50%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Desperate to prove something - watch for burnout.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
