			<personalityDescription>Compromise is just another word for weakness in Scota&apos;s mind. They don&apos;t negotiate or accommodate - they dictate, expecting the world to move according to their vision, whether others like it or not. Scota has seen too much, lost too much, to care anymore. The only thing that matters is getting the job done, and if that means making brutal decisions, so be it. In their world, kindness is just another word for weakness. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sees compromise as failure. Imposes vision regardless of input.&lt;br&gt;- Bleeds others, not themself. Doesn&apos;t lose sleep.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
