			<personalityDescription>Everything grates on him - people, orders, even the sound of his own comms. Hai-feng is always on edge, snapping at allies and enemies alike. Whether it&apos;s stress, trauma, or just who he is, his temper is a fuse ready to blow. Before the mission even begins, Hai-feng has already memorized the terrain, accounted for ammo reserves, and assigned every comrade a secondary role in case the plan goes sideways. &quot;You think too much,&quot; someone mutters. He doesn&apos;t argue. Thinking too much is why he&apos;s still alive. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 52%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Radio chatter sets them off. So do people.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
