			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Malmuirie could probably win more fights if they didn&apos;t spend so much time starting them. Whether it&apos;s trash-talking over comms or throwing the first punch in a negotiation, they seem to believe the best way to solve a problem is by making it someone else&apos;s problem. Fist first. Malmuirie never gives a straight answer. They dodge questions, avoid commitments, and keep people guessing about where they really stands. It&apos;s not outright lying - it&apos;s just never letting anyone get close enough to see the truth. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 46%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Starts problems just to end them violently. First to swing, last to think.&lt;br&gt;- Never commits. Just enough truth to stay slippery.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
