			<personalityDescription>Indecision is just another form of weakness, and Wai-Leng refuses to entertain it. She makes the call, moves forward, and never looks back - because in the brutal reality of war, second-guessing gets people killed. Wai-Leng is the guy who sighs loudly when someone asks a dumb question. She rolls her eyes, mutters under her breath, and gets annoyed over small things - but beneath the grumbling, she still gets the job done. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 42%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sees hesitation as lethal. Makes the call, never looks back. Hard charger.&lt;br&gt;- No time for fools - barely any for friends.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
