			<personalityDescription>Hughie doesn&apos;t measure risk the way others do. Where they see danger, he sees duty; where others hesitate, he moves forward. Not because he doesn&apos;t feel fear, but because he refuses to let it define him. Hughie hates being near &apos;Meks, not because they&apos;re ineffective, but because they&apos;re too effective. Every time he sees one move, he remembers what they leave behind - crushed buildings, burning wreckage, bodies no one ever digs out. &quot;You don&apos;t pilot a &apos;Mek. You unleash one. And when it moves, something always gets left in ruins.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 48%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sees duty, not danger. Fear present - but doesn&apos;t get a say.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
