			<personalityDescription>The more dangerous the path, the more certain Judith is that it&apos;s the right one. She moves forward without fear, seeing every unknown as a puzzle to solve, a victory to claim, or a story to tell later. Judith&apos;s comrades keep dying. Her gear? It stays. So she talks to it, maintains it with care, treats it like it&apos;s alive - because at least it won&apos;t bleed out on her. At least it won&apos;t leave. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 55%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- The harder the path, the more they want it. Danger is proof they&apos;re on track.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
