			<personalityDescription>Enough is never enough for Samuel. He overcommits, overkills, and overcompensates, whether it&apos;s unloading an entire magazine into a crippled enemy or turning a simple job into an all-consuming mission. If restraint is a virtue, Samuel never learned it. Samuel makes it seem like he&apos;s a team player, but everything he does is carefully crafted to benefit himself first. He&apos;s always angling for the best outcome for him, making sure that when the dust settles, he&apos;s the one standing on top. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 41%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Overcommits, overkills, overdoes. Restraint is a foreign concept.&lt;br&gt;- Acts like a team player - until there&apos;s something better on the table.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
