			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Je-ju moves through life with a hardened heart. Death, betrayal, and suffering don&apos;t faze him - they&apos;re just the natural order of things. He does what needs to be done and doesn&apos;t waste time mourning the cost. Before every battle, Je-ju lights a small candle in his quarters or in the corner of a DropShip hangar. It&apos;s always the same scent, something that reminds him of home - wherever that was. He doesn&apos;t talk about it, but those who&apos;ve fought beside him know: it&apos;s not just a habit. It&apos;s a tether, a way to remind himself there&apos;s still a world beyond the blood and steel. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Doesnt flinch, doesnt linger - just keeps walking.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
