			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>For Alfonso, compromise is just another word for weakness. They stick to their principles, strategies, and orders with unwavering determination, even when logic - or survival - suggests a different path. &quot;We&apos;re supposed to trust intel from who?&quot; Alfonso demands, arms crossed. If a plan sounds too clean, they assume it&apos;s wrong. If an enemy retreats too fast, they assume they&apos;re baiting them in. They&apos;re not paranoid, they insist - they&apos;re just still alive. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sees compromise as failure. Principles trump survival instinct.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
