			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Claudio measures everything - risks, rewards, weaknesses - before making a move. To him, emotion is just another factor to manipulate, and hesitation is a flaw he has no intention of indulging. Claudio&apos;s seen too many comrades die. He&apos;s stopped trying to make real connections with people - they never last. But animals? They don&apos;t ask questions. They don&apos;t make promises they can&apos;t keep. And when Claudio whispers to a half-starved dog before a skirmish, telling it to run and hide, it&apos;s not because he&apos;s worried about the mutt. It&apos;s because, deep down, he knows it&apos;ll outlive him. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Emotion is leverage, not weakness. Hesitation isn&apos;t tolerated.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
