			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>There&apos;s no such thing as overconfidence in Ke-huy&apos;s mind. Whether he&apos;s got the skills to back it up or not is irrelevant - he steps into every situation like he&apos;s already won and lets reality catch up later. Ke-huy treats every piece of gear like a lifeline, stockpiling supplies in hidden caches and refusing to part with anything that might prove useful. Even when others go without, he holds tight to what he&apos;s gathered - just in case. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 46%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Confidence exceeds ability. May succeed through force of will - or get others killed.&lt;br&gt;- Has backup caches for backup caches. Won&apos;t crack them open unless dying.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
