			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Diepolt thrives on impulse, driven by an unshakable belief that momentum is more important than caution. Plans are for people who doubt themselves - Diepolt simply does, and lets the universe catch up. Diepolt keeps his hands busy because if they stop, his mind wanders. Back to the names he&apos;s crossed out. Back to the missions that went wrong. So he spins the pen. Over and over. Faster. Slower. Anything to keep his fingers moving, to keep the silence from creeping in. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 50%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Momentum addict. Planning seen as weakness. Lets consequences catch up later.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
