			<personalityDescription>People rally behind Billy because he makes them believe. His confidence, determination, and unwavering presence push others to go beyond their limits, knowing that if he&apos;s leading, victory feels possible. Billy will stop mid-patrol to have a full conversation with a local stray or a scavenger bird perched on a ruined building. His lance teases him for it - until a pack of giant canines doesn&apos;t attack them, or an avian swarm takes off suddenly, giving him just enough warning before an ambush. Maybe Billy&apos;s just lucky. Or maybe the animals know something the rest of them don&apos;t. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 41%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- People push harder when {0} walks in. That&apos;s not luck - that&apos;s leadership.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
