			<personalityDescription>Caution is for the slow and the dead, and Bob refuses to be either. He rushes headlong into danger, making split-second decisions that could be called bravery - or  sheer madness. One way or another, Bob never stands still. After seeing too much death and betrayal, Bob has stopped caring. He doesn&apos;t form attachments, doesn&apos;t believe in causes, and doesn&apos;t waste energy on emotions. In his mind, caring only leads to pain. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 51%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Rejects caution. Speed over safety. Bravery or recklessness - depends on the day.&lt;br&gt;- Seen too much, feels nothing. Not dead - just numb.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
