			<personalityDescription>Once, Caspar might have wanted more, but now? He&apos;s seen too many people claw their way to the top only to die just like everyone else. Ambition is just another word for desperation, and Caspar has long since stopped caring. Caspar&apos;s willingness to cross the line isn&apos;t about ruthlessness - it&apos;s about survival. He&apos;s seen what happens when people hesitate. He&apos;s made the hard calls before, and he&apos;ll make them again, no matter what it costs. &quot;If someone has to suffer so the rest of us make it home, I&apos;ll pull the trigger myself. And I&apos;ll live with it. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Burned out or just gave up - either way, not climbing.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
