			<personalityDescription>Planning has never been Stan&apos;s strong suit. He follows instinct over strategy, letting adrenaline and quick thinking dictate his path. Sometimes it works, sometimes it doesn&apos;t - but either way, he never hesitates. Stan doesn&apos;t fight like a brute, because he refuses to believe war is just violence for violence&apos;s sake. If he doesn&apos;t turn it into something greater, into art, then what is it? Just murder. And he can&apos;t let himself believe that&apos;s all there is. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Strategy ignored. Runs on instinct and adrenaline. Sometimes lucky, always fast.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
