			<personalityDescription>Daniel isn&apos;t satisfied with victory - he demands eradication. To him, an enemy left standing is an enemy that wasn&apos;t taught the right lesson, and he has no interest in teaching it twice. Daniel is the guy who sighs loudly when someone asks a dumb question. He rolls his eyes, mutters under his breath, and gets annoyed over small things - but beneath the grumbling, he still gets the job done. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 48%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Victory is incomplete if anything survives. Believes lessons should be final.&lt;br&gt;- No time for fools - barely any for friends.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
