			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Jing-quo always looks out for number one. If a situation doesn&apos;t benefit him directly, he&apos;s not interested. He&apos;ll work with others when it suits him, but the moment it stops being profitable, he&apos;s already moving on. Jing-quo eats for survival, not pleasure. He&apos;ll consume anything that keeps him moving, from high-energy nutrient bricks to mysterious battlefield leftovers. &quot;Food is fuel,&quot; he shrugs, gnawing on something vaguely resembling jerky. &quot;Doesn&apos;t matter what it is as long as it works.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 46%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Helps when it helps them - otherwise, not their problem.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
