			<personalityDescription>There&apos;s no such thing as overconfidence in Leon&apos;s mind. Whether he&apos;s got the skills to back it up or not is irrelevant - he steps into every situation like he&apos;s already won and lets reality catch up later. Leon measures everything - risks, rewards, weaknesses - before making a move. To him, emotion is just another factor to manipulate, and hesitation is a flaw he has no intention of indulging. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Confidence exceeds ability. May succeed through force of will - or get others killed.&lt;br&gt;- Emotion is leverage, not weakness. Hesitation isn&apos;t tolerated.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
