			<personalityDescription>Subtlety and restraint are foreign concepts to Cheong-sang. He meets every challenge, real or imagined, with immediate intensity, his first instinct always to escalate rather than back down. Cheong-sang doesn&apos;t waste time on moral debates. If cutting corners or bending the rules gets the job done faster, he&apos;ll do it without hesitation. His comrades have learned not to ask how he pulls off certain victories. &quot;Look, I got the result we needed. Let&apos;s not ruin it by asking too many questions.&quot; </personalityDescription>
