			<personalityDescription>Xenophon thrives on impulse, driven by an unshakable belief that momentum is more important than caution. Plans are for people who doubt themselves - Xenophon simply does, and lets the universe catch up. Xenophon keeps everything - ammo, supplies, spare parts - because you never know when you&apos;ll need them. He refuses to let go of anything useful, even if it means stockpiling more than he could ever realistically use. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 56%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Momentum addict. Planning seen as weakness. Lets consequences catch up later.&lt;br&gt;- Keeps everything that isn&apos;t nailed down. Doesn&apos;t share. Doesn&apos;t trust.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
