			<personalityDescription>Frazer knows best - just ask him. Whether it&apos;s battle tactics, logistics, or how to hold a damn coffee cup, he has an opinion and makes sure everyone hears it. If Frazer had more hands, he would probably try to do everyone&apos;s job at the same time. Frazer&apos;s leadership style leaves no room for autonomy. He scrutinizes every action, corrects every mistake before it happens, and exerts his will so thoroughly that those around him rarely get the chance to think for themselves. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Has input on everything. Micromanages down to the trivial.&lt;br&gt;- Smothers autonomy. Others follow not by choice - but by lack of room to do otherwise.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
