			<personalityDescription>Tze-Wei sees rules as obstacles, not boundaries. If there&apos;s a shortcut to be taken or a loophole to exploit, she&apos;ll find it - ethics and fairness be damned. Tze-Wei&apos;s hunger for success, control, or destruction knows no limits. She takes and takes, pushing herself and others past the breaking point, never feeling like it&apos;s enough. Her drive isn&apos;t ambition - it&apos;s addiction. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 41%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Treats rules like suggestions. Never plays clean.&lt;br&gt;- Pushes past limits like they don&apos;t exist. Burnout risk? Doesnt care.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
