			<personalityDescription>With a quick joke and a warm smile, Zeheb turns even the coldest encounters into something comfortable. They treat allies like family and strangers like potential friends, believing that a little kindness can go a long way - even in war. Zeheb knows how cruel the world is. They&apos;ve seen what happens when people stop caring, stop being human. So they cling to formality, to pleasantries, to basic courtesy. They bow their head when passing the dead, murmurs &quot;I&apos;m so sorry&quot; when patching up another wounded warrior. If they stop being polite, they&apos;re afraid of what they&apos;ll become. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 48%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Makes friends faster than most make enemies.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
