			<personalityDescription>Caution is for the weak, and Juanita has no patience for it. She charges headlong into the most dangerous situations with reckless abandon, trusting skill and sheer audacity to carry her through - because hesitation gets people killed. Juanita is always moving - tapping her fingers on her leg, adjusting her gloves, shifting her stance even when in cover. Her lance used to think she was anxious, but no - this is just how she operates. She says she fights better when she&apos;s in motion. And judging by her reaction time, she might actually be right. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Rejects caution. Relies on audacity and instinct. High survivability or quick death.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
