			<personalityDescription>Embarrassment is for other people. Leos takes what he wants, says what he pleases, and never worries about how he&apos;s perceived. If someone doesn&apos;t like it, that&apos;s their problem, not his. While he doesn&apos;t seek attention, Leos notices everything. He listens more than he speaks, analyzes before he acts, and values deep conversations over shallow chatter. His quiet nature makes his words all the more impactful when he chooses to share them. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Doesn&apos;t care how it looks - as long as it works.&lt;br&gt;- Quiet type. Won&apos;t lead the toast, but will notice who&apos;s missing.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
