			<personalityDescription>To Dorothy, control isn&apos;t a preference - it&apos;s a necessity. They dictate every move, barks orders without question, and refuses to tolerate disobedience. In their world, authority isn&apos;t earned - it&apos;s enforced. Dorothy sees people as tools - useful until they&apos;re not. They take what they need, wring every ounce of value out of those around them, and discard them the moment they become dead weight. Loyalty and morality are just obstacles to be overcome. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 40%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Enforces authority, not leadership. Obedience expected, not requested.&lt;br&gt;- Treats people like tools - breaks them, bins them, moves on.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
