			<personalityDescription>Lois&apos;s leadership style leaves no room for autonomy. She scrutinizes every action, corrects every mistake before it happens, and exerts her will so thoroughly that those around her rarely get the chance to think for themselves. Lois doesn&apos;t whine, grumble, or overreact. If something is bad, she deals with it. If something is really bad, she deals with it harder. &quot;Yeah. It&apos;s bad. So let&apos;s fix it.&quot; </personalityDescription>
