			<personalityDescription>Enough is never enough for Akela. He overcommits, overkills, and overcompensates, whether it&apos;s unloading an entire magazine into a crippled enemy or turning a simple job into an all-consuming mission. If restraint is a virtue, Akela never learned it. Akela refuses to see a fight as unwinnable. Outnumbered? That just means more targets. Outgunned? They&apos;ll run out of ammo first. His confidence is unshakable, even when reality says otherwise. &quot;We just need one good break. And trust me - it&apos;s coming.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 59%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Overcommits, overkills, overdoes. Restraint is a foreign concept.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
