			<personalityDescription>Trying to anticipate Nancy&apos;s next move is a waste of time. She follows no pattern, sticks to no script, and seems to act purely on instinct - sometimes brilliant, sometimes reckless, but always unpredictable. Nancy refuses to let war reduce her to grunts and curses. She speaks in layered, precise language because it reminds her that she&apos;s still human. That she&apos;s still thinking. Because the moment she starts speaking like the others - like a killer - she knows there&apos;s nothing left to save. </personalityDescription>
