			<personalityDescription>Samuli doesn&apos;t just want to prove himself - he needs to. He throws himself into battles, pushes limits, and takes on risks that others would shy away from, desperate to show he&apos;s worthy of something bigger. Samuli doesn&apos;t flirt just to entertain himself - he does it because the alternative is silence. He keeps things playful because if he stops, he has to think about what happens when there&apos;s no one left to talk to at all. &quot;Don&apos;t go quiet on me now. Who else am I supposed to charm while the world falls apart?&quot; </personalityDescription>
