			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Subtlety and patience have never been Phuong-Anh&apos;s strengths. They speak before thinking, act before planning, and never apologize for either. If boldness is a virtue, then they consider themself a saint. Phuong-Anh gives out names because it means someone sees you. Military units burn through people fast - warriors, techs, medics, clerks. Most of them get a number on a payroll log and little else. But if Phuong-Anh calls you &apos;Chief&apos; or &apos;Rookie&apos; or &apos;Grimlock,&apos; it means you existed. Even if only for a little while. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- No patience, no filter, no regrets. Speaks and acts before thinking. Owns it.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
