			<personalityDescription>Daniel&apos;s mind is razor-sharp, cutting through noise and distractions to find the truth hidden beneath. He notices patterns, anticipates outcomes, and always seems to be one step ahead of the game. Daniel&apos;s tone alone is enough to set people on edge. Whether it&apos;s the slow, deliberate way he corrects others or the way he smirks when they struggle, he makes it painfully clear that he thinks he&apos;s leagues ahead of everyone else. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Filters out the noise. Cuts straight to what matters.&lt;br&gt;- Even praise feels like punishment. Might make enemies just by talking.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
