			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Mu&apos;mina doesn&apos;t care about honor or fair fights - only winning. She exploits weaknesses, sacrifices pawns when necessary, and always fights on her terms. If the enemy expects a straight fight, they&apos;ve already lost. Mu&apos;mina doesn&apos;t just study the famous battles - she memorizes the names of those no one remembers. The warriors whose units were wiped out, the commands that vanished, the colonies erased by war and never rebuilt. She collects their stories because no one else will. Because one day, someone will have to do the same for her. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- No honor, no hesitation - just results.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
