			<personalityDescription>Iyam doesn&apos;t just look down on others - they barely acknowledge them. They see themself as superior in every way, treating allies as tools and enemies as annoyances. If someone disagrees with them, it&apos;s because they&apos;re too stupid to understand why they&apos;re right. Iyam is always ready for action, diving headfirst into challenges with enthusiasm. Whether it&apos;s a new mission, a tough fight, or a high-stakes gamble, they thrive on the thrill of what&apos;s next. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Barely acknowledges teammates. Sees people as tools or distractions.&lt;br&gt;- First to volunteer - might need a leash.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
