			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>For Edward, every challenge is simply an opportunity to prove just how infallible he is. He dismisses advice and warnings with a smirk, trusting that his skills and luck will always carry him through, no matter the risk. Everyone who works with Edward gets a nickname, and once he assigns one, it&apos;s yours for life. The problem? They don&apos;t always make sense. &quot;Hey, &apos;Wires,&apos; pass me that wrench.&quot; &quot;Edward, I&apos;m not an electrician.&quot; &quot;Don&apos;t argue with me, Wires.&quot; The name sticks. It always sticks. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sees every warning as noise. Trusts skill to bail them out - always.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
