			<personalityDescription>Topan believes that hesitation is just another way to lose. He trusts his instincts, makes the call, and commits fully - because in his mind, the worst decision is no decision at all. While others waste time with diplomacy, Topan gets straight to the point. He values efficiency over politeness and doesn&apos;t believe in dancing around the truth. Some find his approach refreshing - others just find it frustrating. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Trusts instincts over perfection. Believes any action is better than none.&lt;br&gt;- Talks like time is short and patience shorter.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
