			<personalityDescription>Mahon has survived things that should have killed him - more than once. No matter how many times he gets knocked down, he just keeps getting back up, proving that sometimes, sheer refusal to die is a strategy all its own. Mahon doesn&apos;t waste time on moral debates - he does what needs to be done. If that means breaking promises, cutting corners, or stepping over someone to get ahead, so be it. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 69%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Gets knocked down - gets back up. Survival is the tactic.&lt;br&gt;- Gets results, not approval - steps over whoever&apos;s in the way.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
