			<personalityDescription>To Mitchell, honor is just another tool - useful when it suits him, disposable when it doesn&apos;t. He&apos;s not bound by loyalty or ideals, only by what benefits him most in the moment. Mitchell has watched people break because they weren&apos;t ready to endure real hardship. He&apos;s seen them fail when things got too rough, collapse when the pressure hit. He refuses to be one of them. Pain isn&apos;t just necessary - it&apos;s the price of survival. </personalityDescription>
