			<personalityDescription>Good enough is never good enough for Mildred. She grind herself to the bone, pushing past exhaustion, knowing that even the slightest lapse in preparation could mean failure - or death. She doesn&apos;t stop, because stopping means weakness. Mildred doesn&apos;t do favors, fight for causes, or make sacrifices for free. If someone needs her skills, they&apos;d better be ready to pay up, because when the money stops, so does her interest. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 54%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Pushes past limits. Believes stopping is the first step to failure.&lt;br&gt;- Doesn&apos;t move unless the C-Bills do. Motivation ends where the payment does.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
