			<personalityDescription>Yen-Meng doesn&apos;t believe in aimless effort - every action, every decision serves a purpose. She keeps her eyes on the prize, unwilling to let anything pull her off course. Yen-Meng&apos;s storage room isn&apos;t just crates and tools - it&apos;s also full of plants. &quot;They help with air quality,&quot; she says, watering a row of succulents next to a rack of medical supplies. Everyone lets it slide because, honestly? It does make the place feel less miserable. </personalityDescription>
