			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Ming doesn&apos;t do safe. He thrives in the unknown, the uncertain, the dangerous - where risk is high and the rewards even higher. Whether it&apos;s luck, skill, or sheer nerve, he always seems to come out the other side with a grin. Ming doesn&apos;t just maintain his gear - he talks to it. &quot;Alright, sweetheart, let&apos;s not jam on me today.&quot; His sidearm gets a pep talk before every battle, and his knife? He&apos;s got a name for that, too. His lance has stopped questioning it - it seems to work. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 52%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Avoids safety by choice. Risk is the goal. Somehow, keeps surviving.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
