			<personalityDescription>Caution is for the slow and the dead, and Reginald refuses to be either. He rushes headlong into danger, making split-second decisions that could be called bravery - or  sheer madness. One way or another, Reginald never stands still. Reginald&apos;s clothes don&apos;t fit the war-torn world he lives in. His coats are pristine, his accessories impractical, his boots polished like he&apos;s about to attend a grand ball instead of supporting a military unit. He dresses like he&apos;s from a world that hasn&apos;t existed in centuries - as if, by refusing to acknowledge reality, he can pretend it still does. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 55%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Rejects caution. Speed over safety. Bravery or recklessness - depends on the day.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
