			<personalityDescription>Enough is never enough for Kateb. He overcommits, overkills, and overcompensates, whether it&apos;s unloading an entire magazine into a crippled enemy or turning a simple job into an all-consuming mission. If restraint is a virtue, Kateb never learned it. In a brutal world where hope is a rare commodity, Kateb refuses to let it die. Even when everything is crumbling, his words, actions, and sheer force of will remind others that there&apos;s still something worth fighting for. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 57%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Overcommits, overkills, overdoes. Restraint is a foreign concept.&lt;br&gt;- Has a way of making the impossible feel inevitable.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
