			<personalityDescription>Some people call it grit, others call it madness, but Louisa doesn&apos;t care what they think. No matter how much the world tries to grind her down, she keeps going, long after anyone else would have quit. Louisa insists that every uniform, flight suit, and cooling vest is properly fitted before deployment. If she sees a tech in a grease-stained jumpsuit with an undone collar, they&apos;ll get an earful - because a ragged warrior is a careless one, and carelessness gets people killed. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 52%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Grit or madness - hard to tell. Doesn&apos;t care. Just keeps moving.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
