			<personalityDescription>Compassion is a weakness Kang-min can&apos;t afford. They don&apos;t hesitate to make hard decisions, sacrifice allies, or eliminate threats with cold efficiency. In their mind, survival means shutting out anything that might make them hesitate. Kang-min is good at their job, but they&apos;ll never admit it. No matter how well they manage things, they act like a single misstep could doom the entire unit. They&apos;ll triple-check orders, then apologize for bothering people about them. If you thank them, they&apos;ll probably just say, &quot;Oh, it wasn&apos;t much, really. Sorry if it was.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 48%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Cuts ties as easily as throats - doesn&apos;t blink.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
