			<personalityQuirkDescriptionIndex>0</personalityQuirkDescriptionIndex>
			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Once, Vitol&apos;d might have cared. Now, he just drifts. Wars rage, alliances shift, people come and go, and none of it moves him. He does what&apos;s necessary to get by, but passion and purpose are long-forgotten luxuries. Vitol&apos;d never stands too close to a &apos;Mek, never trusts that they&apos;re fully powered down, never walks beneath one without his pulse spiking. They&apos;re too big, too unnatural, too much like monsters pretending to be machines. &quot;I don&apos;t care if it&apos;s offline. That thing&apos;s one bad signal away from flattening this entire place.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 50%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Burned out long before we met them. Just ash in uniform.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
