			<performanceExamScore>53</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Every insult, every disagreement, every minor inconvenience is a personal attack in Jeanne&apos;s mind. She holds grudges for years, going out of her way to make sure anyone who crosses her regrets it, even if it costs her more than it&apos;s worth. Jeanne&apos;s paranoia isn&apos;t about efficiency - it&apos;s about survival. She&apos;s seen how fast things spiral when someone gets lazy. A rushed approval. A miscalculated order. A misfiled name on a casualty report. She checks and rechecks because one mistake can&apos;t be undone. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Thinks a cold shoulder counts as tactical retaliation.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
